any each has; a quad or textured export goes out whole), and the preview counts what goes out as "40k of 81k triangles"; for the 3D print, **Hollow for this file only** (off at first; settings file `export_hollow`), with its **Wall** beside it (2 mm at first, 0.5 to 20 mm; settings file `export_hollow_wall`), which writes each object with an inside wall that thick facing the hollow, as resin slicers hollow a model (the slicer adds the drain holes): the object becomes voxels two fifths of the wall across in a copy, the surface the wall's depth inside it is meshed and added, decimated to the object's triangles when it has more, and a part thinner than two walls stays solid; the preview says "Hollow inside a 2.0 mm wall" (and when the wall is under Settings' least wall, says so), a wall too thin for an object that big (over about 400 walls across) is refused with a note, and the print's note gives the hollow solid's volume; for a mesh the selected object, its vertices and what the format carries; the link's folder, or where to set it; Turntable's frames and Without background; Picture's Render it (Scene > Render's switch, with Fast or Full) and Without background; the scene's Save as or Save a copy. On the right, the preview: the object's thumbnail (the view's middle for the scene, a picture or a turntable), the file name the dialog will suggest (the scene's name with the format's suffix, or Untitled), what goes in, its triangles and about how big, and a print's width, depth and height (of all its objects together). The foot says what Export does to the scene ("Exports a copy; the scene is not changed", or for Save as that the new file becomes the scene's own), then Cancel and Export. Export runs the format's own command, so each writes what it always did, and a mesh or print format's save dialog offers only that format. A preset comes back on the format last picked in it; the sheet opens on what was exported last, which its head names ("Last time: glTF for the game engine"), or on 3D print before anything has been. The settings file keeps `export_preset`, `export_format`, `export_ran`, `export_last_preset` and `export_last_format` (an older file's `export_format` settles into the first preset that offers it); Esc closes the sheet. **Before it prints** (`src/app/print_checks.odin`): under the preview of a 3D print stand its checks, each a tick or a warning: Watertight (every edge has two faces; or how many open edges, edges of more than two faces or flipped, or that it is inside out), its holes, with **Repair** (Close holes on every hole, one undo step), its thinnest wall against the least set in Settings > Files > 3D printer (rays from 4096 triangles spread over the surface go inward to the far side of the wall, and the third thinnest decides, so a stray pinch does not; measured once the surface is closed), and whether it fits the printer's bed, turned a quarter round if need be. They look at what the file holds (the shown level, a dynamic object's packed triangles or a voxel object's surface) and run again only when it changes; above 300k triangles they run on a thread of their own from a copy, the rows saying "Checking the print..." meanwhile (about 0.6 s at 2M triangles in a release build on four cores), and above 4M triangles they are left out. With more than one object going out, the checks are of the selected one, which the caption names, and the bed check holds them all. Exit stats: `export_open`, `export_preset`, `export_format`, `export_runs`, `export_last` (`none` before an export), `export_print_all`, `export_decimate`, `export_decimate_to` and `export_decimated` (the triangles the last decimated export wrote), `export_hollow`, `export_hollow_wall` and `export_hollowed` (the triangles the last hollow print's inside walls added). The checks add `print_checks` (checks begun), `print_open_edges`, `print_holes`, `print_wall` (in the object's units, 0 for none), `print_check_ms`, `print_bed` and `print_wall_least`. Every f